[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4951469379","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121133#issuecomment-4951469379","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121133","id":4951469379,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJyFtQw","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-12T14:07:08Z","updated_at":"2026-07-12T14:07:08Z","body":"I'm not convinced by this solution. You can trigger the same issue with other tokens as well, e.g.\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nif a2$all():\r\n    pass\r\n```\r\n\r\nI don't think solving this in the expression parser makes sense, because it would imply that the expression parsing greedily consumes tokens that might be relevant to some context in which expressions can appear. As you correctly pointed out the error might be a bit misleading. So what we should do IMO is rephrase the error messages to e.g. \"Found unexpected `..` after if condition, expected `:`.\" Also the error location seems to be not correctly set, we should address that as well.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4951469379/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4954419940","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121133#issuecomment-4954419940","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121133","id":4954419940,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJ05y5A","user":{"login":"Chaganti-Reddy","id":97330178,"node_id":"U_kgDOBc0kAg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97330178?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy","html_url":"https://github.com/Chaganti-Reddy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-13T04:25:08Z","updated_at":"2026-07-13T04:25:37Z","body":"> I'm not convinced by this solution. You can trigger the same issue with other tokens as well, e.g.\r\n> \r\n> ```gdscript\r\n> if a2$all():\r\n>     pass\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> I don't think solving this in the expression parser makes sense, because it would imply that the expression parsing greedily consumes tokens that might be relevant to some context in which expressions can appear. As you correctly pointed out the error might be a bit misleading. So what we should do IMO is rephrase the error messages to e.g. \"Found unexpected `..` after if condition, expected `:`.\" Also the error location seems to be not correctly set, we should address that as well.\r\n\r\nyeah that makes sense, you're right. I didn't think about the greedy-consuming part, and like you said the same thing happens with `$` (and probably other tokens too), so patching just `..` in the expression parser was too narrow anyway.\r\n\r\nI'll drop the expression parser change and instead fix it at `consume()` so the error names the token that was actually found (like your \"Found unexpected `..` after if condition, expected `:`\") and set the location to point at that token instead.\r\n\r\none quick question before I redo it: do you want this done generally inside `consume()` so every \"expected X\" error reports what it actually found, or keep it scoped to just these condition messages? happy to do the general one if that's preferred.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4954419940/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4956167359","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121133#issuecomment-4956167359","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121133","id":4956167359,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJ2kcvw","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-13T08:54:49Z","updated_at":"2026-07-13T08:54:49Z","body":"I think we should keep that out of `consume`, in general the generic utils leave error handling to more specific callers. This makes it easier to improve on specific errors, without having to adjust everything.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4956167359/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4956492462","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121133#issuecomment-4956492462","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121133","id":4956492462,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJ24Srg","user":{"login":"Chaganti-Reddy","id":97330178,"node_id":"U_kgDOBc0kAg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97330178?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy","html_url":"https://github.com/Chaganti-Reddy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaganti-Reddy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-13T09:31:20Z","updated_at":"2026-07-13T09:31:20Z","body":"> I think we should keep that out of `consume`, in general the generic utils leave error handling to more specific callers. This makes it easier to improve on specific errors, without having to adjust everything.\r\n\r\ntook your approach - dropped the `expression-parser` change entirely and instead handle it at the specific callers (for/if/while), so the error now names the token actually found and points the location at it. e.g. `if a2$all():` now gives `Expected \":\" after \"if\" condition, found \"$\" instead.` kept it out of consume like you said. updated the missing_colon test for the new wording and added one for the reported `..` case.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4956492462/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4983240063","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121133#issuecomment-4983240063","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121133","id":4983240063,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKQY1fw","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5